{#
  The patient queue table for one trial.

  Extracted into its own partial for two reasons: pass 2 renders exactly this
  fragment inside a <turbo-frame> to poll for status changes, and keeping it
  separate means the polled markup and the first-render markup can never drift
  apart. There is one source of truth for a row.

  Expects: trial, patients, latest (evaluations keyed by person_id), counts,
           hasActive.

  ── The rule this table follows ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  A row's action is DERIVED from the data, never remembered by the browser:

      no evaluation          → offer "Queue"
      pending / running      → show the status, offer nothing
      completed / failed     → show the status, offer "Re-run"

  That is why the button genuinely disappears after queueing and stays gone
  across a refresh, a back-navigation, or someone else queueing the same patient
  in another tab. Disabling a button in JavaScript would come undone on reload;
  this cannot.
#}
{#
  data-active is the poller's stop signal, and it is deliberately INSIDE the
  frame: Turbo replaces a frame's children, never the frame element's own
  attributes, so a flag on the wrapper would freeze at its first-render value and
  the loop would never terminate. Living here, it is re-read after every refresh
  and the server stays the authority on whether work is outstanding.
#}
<div class="status-summary"
     data-evaluation-poll-target="state"
     data-active="{{ hasActive ? 'true' : 'false' }}">
  {#
    ONE polite live region for the whole table, not one per cell. A screen reader
    announcing a hundred individually-changing status cells is unusable noise; a
    single sentence that says what changed is genuinely useful. Pass 2's poller
    replaces this element's contents, and the announcement follows for free.
  #}
  <p aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" class="muted">
    {% if counts.queued == 0 %}
      No evaluations queued for this trial yet.
    {% else %}
      {{ counts.queued }} of {{ patients|length }} patient{{ patients|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} queued ·
      {{ counts.active }} in progress ·
      {{ counts.completed }} completed{% if counts.failed > 0 %} · {{ counts.failed }} failed{% endif %}.
    {% endif %}
  </p>

  {#
    Bulk queue. Lives inside the frame, next to the counts it depends on, so the
    number on the button stays truthful as rows are queued elsewhere rather than
    going stale at whatever it was when the page first loaded.

    Only ever queues patients with NO evaluation yet — never re-runs a finished
    one. That keeps the button safe to press twice: the second press finds
    nothing remaining and says so.
  #}
  {% if remaining > 0 %}
    <form method="post" action="{{ path('lumina_ui_evaluation_queue_all') }}"
          onsubmit="return confirm('Queue evaluations for {{ remaining }} patient{{ remaining == 1 ? '' : 's' }} against this trial?');">
      <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('queue-all-' ~ trial.id) }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="trial_id" value="{{ trial.id }}">
      <button type="submit">
        Queue all {{ remaining }} remaining patient{{ remaining == 1 ? '' : 's' }}
      </button>
      {# The confirm() above is an enhancement, not a guard — with JavaScript off
         it simply does not fire and the form posts. The action is idempotent in
         the ways that matter, so that is an acceptable trade rather than a hole. #}
    </form>
  {% elseif patients is not empty %}
    <p class="muted">Every patient has an evaluation for this trial. Use “Re-run” on a row to run one again.</p>
  {% endif %}
</div>

{% if patients is empty %}
  <p class="muted">
    No patients found. Check that the patient database is reachable and that
    <code>PATIENT_DATABASE_URL</code> is set correctly.
  </p>
{% else %}
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <caption>
        {{ patients|length }} patient{{ patients|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} ·
        queue each one against {{ trial.studyId ?? ('trial ' ~ trial.id) }}
      </caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Patient</th>
          <th scope="col">Age</th>
          <th scope="col">Condition</th>
          <th scope="col">ECOG</th>
          <th scope="col">Status</th>
          <th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Actions</span></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for patient in patients %}
          {% set evaluation = latest[patient.personId] ?? null %}
          {# The id is the redirect target after queueing, so the browser puts
             you back on this row instead of the top of the page. #}
          <tr id="patient-{{ patient.personId }}">
            <th scope="row">
              {{ patient.displayName }}
              <span class="muted">({{ patient.personId }})</span>
            </th>

            <td>
              {% set age = patient.approximateAge %}
              {# "approx." is not padding: with only a birth year we can be a year
                 out, and a clinical screen should not imply precision it lacks. #}
              {{ age is null ? '—' : 'approx. ' ~ age }}
            </td>

            <td>
              {% if patient.hasClinicalSummary %}
                {{ patient.disease ?? '—' }}{% if patient.stage %} · stage {{ patient.stage }}{% endif %}
              {% else %}
                <span class="muted">No clinical data recorded</span>
              {% endif %}
            </td>

            {# ECOG 0 is a real, meaningful score ("fully active") — test for null
               explicitly so it never renders as an em dash. #}
            <td>{{ patient.ecogPerformanceStatus is null ? '—' : patient.ecogPerformanceStatus }}</td>

            <td>
              {% if evaluation is null %}
                <span class="muted">Not queued</span>
              {% else %}
                {# The badge carries the word, not just a colour — colour alone
                   fails for colour-blind users and in high-contrast modes. #}
                <span class="badge badge--{{ evaluation.status.value }}">{{ evaluation.status.label }}</span>
                <a href="{{ path('lumina_ui_evaluation_show', {id: evaluation.id}) }}">
                  <span class="visually-hidden">View evaluation for {{ patient.displayName }}, </span>#{{ evaluation.id }}
                </a>
              {% endif %}
            </td>

            <td>
              {% if evaluation is null or evaluation.status.isTerminal %}
                <form method="post" action="{{ path('lumina_ui_evaluation_queue') }}" class="inline">
                  {# Token scoped to this trial AND this patient, so a form cannot
                     be replayed against a different row. #}
                  <input type="hidden" name="_token"
                         value="{{ csrf_token('queue-' ~ trial.id ~ '-' ~ patient.personId) }}">
                  <input type="hidden" name="trial_id" value="{{ trial.id }}">
                  <input type="hidden" name="person_id" value="{{ patient.personId }}">
                  <button type="submit">
                    {{ evaluation is null ? 'Queue' : 'Re-run' }}
                    {# Thirty buttons all named "Queue" are impossible to tell
                       apart in a screen reader's element list. #}
                    <span class="visually-hidden">evaluation for {{ patient.displayName }}</span>
                  </button>
                </form>
              {% else %}
                <span class="muted">
                  Queued
                  <span class="visually-hidden">— no action available for {{ patient.displayName }} while it runs</span>
                </span>
              {% endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
{% endif %}
